==============================================================================
PART A -- the gauge: Watson data depends on D alone (invariant); C0 covariant
==============================================================================
                     p   D         C0   p->3p: C0   ratio  sector pi(1+D)
                   v-1   1     1.0000      3.0000   3.000           6.283
                 v^2+1   2     1.0000      3.0000   3.000           9.425
              v^3-3v+2   3     2.0000      6.0000   3.000          12.566
                2v^4+v   4     2.0000      6.0000   3.000          15.708
  C0 scales EXACTLY by |c|=3 under p->3p (gauge-covariant); the sector opening
  pi(1+D) depends on D only (gauge-invariant). So the per-component (per-degree)
  Watson lemma descends to the gauge quotient.

